# .trivyignore — expiring vulnerability-scan exceptions (SEC-44 policy).
#
# Gate semantics: the pipeline fails on TRIVY_GATE_SEVERITY findings that
# have an available fix (--ignore-unfixed keeps unpatchable OS noise out of
# the gate; unfixed HIGH/CRITICAL findings are listed in the job summary).
# Entries here suppress a finding in EVERY report — gate and SARIF alike —
# so each one must carry all three comment fields immediately above it and
# is enforced by .github/scripts/check-trivyignore.sh (runs in ci.yml and
# inside the scan jobs themselves):
#
#   # reason:   <why the finding is accepted / mitigation>
#   # approver: <github handle>
#   # expires:  YYYY-MM-DD   (≤ 30 days ahead)
#
# Exceptions expire: a past `expires:` fails the check, and the scan jobs
# run trivy against a generated effective ignorefile that drops expired
# entries and pins each survivor with trivy's native `exp:` — expiry is
# enforced at scan time, not just in the lint job. Re-approve with a new
# date instead of deleting history when an exception is still needed.
